htmlcov/

# Secrets / local config — NEVER commit. The scanners (gitleaks) are the backstop, not the
# plan: a secret that reaches a remote branch is compromised even after a force-push, so it
# must not be committable in the first place. PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL in particular carries a
# token in the URL itself.
.env
*.local
secrets.*
*.session
*.key
*.pem
.pypirc

# CI reports
*.test.xml
